  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Thermal decomposition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;produces two paramagnetic gases. The total number of electrons present in the antibonding molecular orbitals of the gas that has the higher number of unpaired electrons is _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mover><mn>2</mn><mi>Ag</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Both the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gases are paramagnetic. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> unpaired electron and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> unpaired electrons. According to MOT, electronic configuration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><msubsup><mo>*</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><msubsup><mo>*</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msubsup><mo>*</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msubsup><mo>*</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup></math></p><p>Total number of electrons present in antibonding molecular orbitals <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
